WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.136
-Our next guest is a talented
actress and comedian

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:05.371
you know from her work on
"Saturday Night Live"

00:00:05.371 --> 00:00:06.405
and "Search Party."

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:07.940
She stars in
"Father of the Bride,"

00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.243
which premieres June 16th
on HBO Max.

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:11.577
Let's take a look.

00:00:11.577 --> 00:00:13.479
-Whatever she wants.

00:00:13.479 --> 00:00:15.347
-I love that. That's beautiful.

00:00:15.347 --> 00:00:17.217
But keep in mind that you never
want to put a bride

00:00:17.217 --> 00:00:18.584
in a dress she can't afford.

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:24.357
So prices usually range
from about here to here.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.959
So where do we land?

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:31.197
-How about there?

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:38.237
-Please welcome to the show
Chloe Fineman, everyone.

00:00:38.237 --> 00:00:40.373
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.373 --> 00:00:46.212 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:52.051 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:52.051 --> 00:00:53.486
Welcome.
Thank you for being here, Chloe.

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.854
-Oh, thank you for having me.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.324
-Congratulations on another
excellent season of "SNL."

00:00:58.324 --> 00:00:59.759
-We did it.
-You did it.

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.195
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:02.195 --> 00:01:05.498
-I feel like your tenure
at the show

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:07.800
has been over
a very difficult time.

00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:11.104
And it's finally getting back to
a little bit of normalcy.

00:01:11.104 --> 00:01:14.173
You guys had the actual --
the party after the finale.

00:01:14.173 --> 00:01:18.210
-Yeah, we had an after party
in the ice-skating rink/

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.746
now it's a roller rink.
-It's a roller-Skating rink.

00:01:19.746 --> 00:01:21.847
-The cool roller-skating rink.
-Yeah.

00:01:21.847 --> 00:01:24.483
-And I'd never experienced that
before. It was wild.

00:01:24.483 --> 00:01:27.320
-And it was always historically
where the party was.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.089
My years, I felt like
every year, it rained.

00:01:30.089 --> 00:01:31.424
That was not the problem
this year.

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:34.660
-No, it was about 120 degrees
outside.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:36.495
-Did you feel like --
Was it a sweaty night?

00:01:36.495 --> 00:01:40.466
-I was in, like,
a thin gold fabric

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:43.001
that kinds of holds smell,
which I didn't realize.

00:01:43.001 --> 00:01:45.538
And it's the end of the year,
and you've bonded with

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.608
all these people, and you're
hugging everybody and saying

00:01:48.608 --> 00:01:52.378
how proud you are, and I had
a big hug with Lorne, you know,

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:53.779
thanking him
for such a great year.

00:01:53.779 --> 00:01:55.748
And then I walked over,
and my best friend was like,

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.283
"I say this as your friend.

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.118
You have never smelled worse."

00:01:59.118 --> 00:02:02.254
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:05.858
-Now, I will say, like,
a really good friend says it

00:02:05.858 --> 00:02:08.328
before you hug your boss.
-Yeah, boss.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:10.964
You know, there's celebs.
We won't name-drop.

00:02:10.964 --> 00:02:14.767
Ronan Farrow -- I'm like,
"We should get a drink."

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.369
-And then you mentioned
your friend.

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.737
These were sort of
growing-up friends

00:02:17.737 --> 00:02:18.938
that you brought to the party.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:21.540
I mean, that is a really cool
party to bring --

00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:24.510
-Yes, yeah, about the coolest
thing you can do.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.679
-And did you take them to
the party after the party?

00:02:26.679 --> 00:02:27.814
-Oh, yeah.
-Alright.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:29.315
-Oh, yeah.
-So did you kind of, like,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:30.850
do it up when you brought
your friends?

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.218
-Yes, I was like,
"Come to this after --"

00:02:33.218 --> 00:02:36.789
Maya Rudolph is singing.
You know, they're dancing.

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:41.027
And then around 6:30, it starts
to kind of -- maybe it was 6:00

00:02:41.027 --> 00:02:43.796
it, like, shuts down, and then
there's the after-after party.

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.130
And I get to be like,

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:49.068
"Guys, want to go hang at Kenan
Thompson's after-after?"

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.936
You know, and they were like,
"What is your life?

00:02:50.936 --> 00:02:52.639
This is so cool."

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:55.441
You know, the show,
it's like this,

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:56.843
and on this night,
you get to celebrate.

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:59.478
So I was like,
"I got it. I got it."

00:02:59.478 --> 00:03:01.714
And it was at
the Hard Rock Hotel.

00:03:01.714 --> 00:03:04.517
Not to give anything away.
He doesn't live there.

00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:07.786
That's just where the party was,
if you want to stalk.

00:03:07.786 --> 00:03:10.522
So I was like, "I got the car,
I got the car."

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.791
So I got, like,
the black UberXL.

00:03:12.791 --> 00:03:14.126
I was going to,
like, you know --

00:03:14.126 --> 00:03:16.095
-Yeah, show it off. Yeah.
-Pimp it up.

00:03:16.095 --> 00:03:18.097
And I get the address,
and we show up.

00:03:18.097 --> 00:03:22.468
And then I accidentally Ubered
us to the Hard Rock T-shirt shop

00:03:22.468 --> 00:03:27.207
at 6:30 in the morning in
the worst part of Times Square.

00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:30.609
-Yeah.
-Like, Elmo was, like, hanging

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:34.313
off the -- You don't want to see
Elmo take the head off.

00:03:34.313 --> 00:03:36.348
-Elmo's like,
"I only take it off now

00:03:36.348 --> 00:03:37.883
'cause nobody comes here."

00:03:37.883 --> 00:03:40.186
-Yeah, and I'm in my gold dress
and I look --

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.987
-This is your beautiful --
-Yeah, this is me.

00:03:41.987 --> 00:03:44.190
-This is not someone that should
be seeing Elmo at 6:30.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:48.394
-No. No, the photo looks
as drunk as I was.

00:03:48.394 --> 00:03:52.665
-We should note, you're carrying
your shoes, the telltale sign

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.833
of someone who's up at 6:30
in the morning.

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.269
-Yes, and sometimes we have fun
paparazzo.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:04:01.441
And this woman said that I
looked like an undone woman.

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:02.542
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:04.977
She was like,
"This is, like, feminism.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:06.678
Do you mind if I take a --"
Yeah.

00:04:06.678 --> 00:04:09.849
-An undone woman sounds like --
I don't know.

00:04:09.849 --> 00:04:12.117
Seems like something Cary Grant
would say to somebody.

00:04:12.117 --> 00:04:14.953
-Yeah, yeah. It was very --
Yeah, my friend Grace Shaker

00:04:14.953 --> 00:04:19.024
saw me just like, "Okay, take
my picture, I guess," you know.

00:04:19.024 --> 00:04:22.528
-You did a wonderful sketch on
the show that I want to ask you

00:04:22.528 --> 00:04:24.830
about called "The Understudy"
where you did

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:27.232
impressions of
your cast members.

00:04:27.232 --> 00:04:29.034
-Mm-hmm.
-And, I mean,

00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:30.703
it makes sense to me, yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:30.703 --> 00:04:33.305
-Thank you. Oh, yeah, yeah. Wow.

00:04:33.305 --> 00:04:37.309
-So, I think, because you are
such a talented impressionist,

00:04:37.309 --> 00:04:40.379
it does not surprise me that you
would have an ear for the people

00:04:40.379 --> 00:04:42.014
you work with and spend the most
time with.

00:04:42.014 --> 00:04:45.351
Were they all aware
that you had them?

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:46.952
-No.
-Okay.

00:04:46.952 --> 00:04:49.355
[ Laughter ]
Did they all react the same?

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:52.057
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.057 --> 00:04:56.695
I was like -- So, Mike DiCenzo
and some writers --

00:04:56.695 --> 00:04:57.830
-Yeah, great writers.

00:04:57.830 --> 00:04:59.165
-They were like,
"We got this idea."

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.534
And I was, like, the most
nervous I've ever been

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:04.269
at a table read 'cause they
don't know I do this.

00:05:04.269 --> 00:05:06.606
And I don't think Kate was
at that table read.

00:05:06.606 --> 00:05:10.109
So the first time she saw me do
the impression was dressed

00:05:10.109 --> 00:05:13.980
as her with the glasses and the
stripes and the wig, just, like,

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.783
"Do you like it?"
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.783 --> 00:05:21.153
-We had -- I mean, Hader -- Over
the years, we found out that,

00:05:21.153 --> 00:05:24.189
like, Hader did have
one of everyone.

00:05:24.189 --> 00:05:26.158
-Really?
-He didn't really show it off

00:05:26.158 --> 00:05:28.594
until -- You would hear sort of
like through back channels,

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:30.496
like, "oh, my God, you got to
see Bill's you."

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:33.332
And I'm like, "Why hasn't he
shown me?"

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:35.668
-Right. 'Cause it's scary.
-It is scary.

00:05:35.668 --> 00:05:37.269
-Yeah, Kate was like...

00:05:37.269 --> 00:05:39.105
[as McKinnon] "How long have you
been sitting on this?"

00:05:39.105 --> 00:05:40.272
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.272 --> 00:05:41.641
Oh!

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:44.243
[ Normal voice ] You know?
She kept calling me a witch.

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:47.847
-Being called a witch by
Kate McKinnon is really nice.

00:05:47.847 --> 00:05:49.882
That's like a compliment,
I think.

00:05:49.882 --> 00:05:51.284
-[ as McKinnon ]
"You little witch."

00:05:51.284 --> 00:05:53.653
[ Laughter ]

00:05:53.653 --> 00:05:56.723
-This is very awkward 'cause I
think sometimes there's that

00:05:56.723 --> 00:05:58.958
thing where two talented
impressionists,

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:01.326
like yourself and me...
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.326 --> 00:06:03.295
...we do the same person,

00:06:03.295 --> 00:06:05.198
and then it's like
who's going to do --

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:08.835
like, if there's a sketch, like,
who's going to do Anna Delvey?

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:10.903
'Cause, like, we both have
such good ones.

00:06:10.903 --> 00:06:11.971
-Right, right.

00:06:11.971 --> 00:06:13.606
-I feel like I should do mine
first.

00:06:13.606 --> 00:06:15.908
-Please.
-Okay.

00:06:15.908 --> 00:06:17.443
[ As Anna Delvey ]
Do you know who I am?

00:06:17.443 --> 00:06:19.144
[ Laughter ]

00:06:19.144 --> 00:06:22.548
The banks are closed in Europe.
I'll send you a wire transfer.

00:06:22.548 --> 00:06:24.116
[ Normal voice ] Right?
-Okay. That's great.

00:06:24.116 --> 00:06:26.185
-So let's hear yours. Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.185 --> 00:06:29.288
-I mean, where were you
when we did the --

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:32.792
-I mean, I feel like this is --
Lorne is very shortsighted.

00:06:32.792 --> 00:06:34.527
I know he's like a genius,
but the fact that he's, like --

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:35.861
-No one told me. I'm upset.

00:06:35.861 --> 00:06:38.497
-He gave it to you because you
looked more like her.

00:06:38.497 --> 00:06:40.899
-We should have put you
in a wig.

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:44.103
-I am her. You look like her.
But give us a little.

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:47.105
-[ As Anna Delvey ]
You look poor. You look poor.

00:06:47.105 --> 00:06:52.344
Being on "Seth Meyers" is
very exclusive and very V.I.P.

00:06:52.344 --> 00:06:55.981
-The fact that you made "poor" a
three-syllable word is really --

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:58.217
[ Laughter ]
'Cause she's like --

00:06:58.217 --> 00:07:01.854
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:05.124
So, this is -- You're in
"Father of the Bride."

00:07:05.124 --> 00:07:07.659
And you are -- this is sort of
the Marty Short --

00:07:07.659 --> 00:07:09.361
the role that Marty Short
made famous.

00:07:09.361 --> 00:07:11.664
-[ Normal voice ] Yeah, the
wedding planner. Yes, yes.

00:07:11.664 --> 00:07:14.834
-And you've gotten to -- you did
a sketch with Marty Short.

00:07:14.834 --> 00:07:16.902
He played Doug Emhoff.
-And I played Ella.

00:07:16.902 --> 00:07:18.070
So we did meet.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:20.773
That was pre-me playing
a wedding planner.

00:07:20.773 --> 00:07:24.943
-Yes. And did you do wedding
planning research for this?

00:07:24.943 --> 00:07:29.081
-You know, I --
It's Netflix, baby, you know?

00:07:29.081 --> 00:07:32.385
It's like the Wikipedia
of the day.

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:35.754
I don't know. Is that so the
dumbest thing I've ever said?

00:07:35.754 --> 00:07:38.891
-It's making me feel dumb
'cause I have no idea

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.793
what you're trying to say.

00:07:40.793 --> 00:07:42.895
-You, like, Google, you know.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:07:42.895 --> 00:07:44.163
-Or like wedding planner,
Wikipedia.

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.198
-So you didn't go follow
a bunch of wedding planners.

00:07:46.198 --> 00:07:48.100
-No, I'm just like,
"Netflix has it."

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:51.337
-Oh, I see. So you just watched
a lot of wedding-planner films.

00:07:51.337 --> 00:07:54.740
-There are so many shows, yeah,
and there's like, weird reality

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.608
television shows
about wedding planning.

00:07:56.608 --> 00:07:57.743
-That's true. This day and age,

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.811
nobody has to go in deep cover
to learn.

00:07:59.811 --> 00:08:02.247
-Totally. And then weirdly,
"The Home Edit" --

00:08:02.247 --> 00:08:03.815
Anyone know "The Home Edit"?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:03.815 --> 00:08:06.885
Whoo-hoo, yes! Container store!

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:08.354
Yay!

00:08:08.354 --> 00:08:09.788
They were so organized.

00:08:09.788 --> 00:08:12.625
So I was like,
"That will kind of inform me."

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:15.094
And then they have assistants,

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:16.895
and I was like,
"Oh, that could be fun."

00:08:16.895 --> 00:08:20.699
I'm just bragging now,
but I got my best friend to play

00:08:20.699 --> 00:08:23.869
my assistant in the movie
because of "The Home Edit."

00:08:23.869 --> 00:08:25.170
Inspiring.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:27.573
[ Applause ]
-Yeah.

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:30.309
-And you had to, like, make up
for that whole Hard Rock fiasco.

00:08:30.309 --> 00:08:32.478
-Right. Yeah.

00:08:32.478 --> 00:08:34.580
-The last thing I want to ask
you about is,

00:08:34.580 --> 00:08:38.183
your dad did improv comedy.
-Yeah.

00:08:38.183 --> 00:08:39.751
-And still does? Does he still?

00:08:39.751 --> 00:08:41.554
-Oh, yeah, baby.
-That's awesome.

00:08:41.554 --> 00:08:44.356
-Uh-huh.
-By the way, I'm so worried.

00:08:44.356 --> 00:08:46.792
Aren't you worried that our kids
are going to react that way

00:08:46.792 --> 00:08:49.494
when people are like, "Your
dad's a comedian?" Like, "Ugh."

00:08:49.494 --> 00:08:52.864
-Yeah, but, like, are you doing
prov three days a week?

00:08:52.864 --> 00:08:55.534
-I'm not prov'ing anymore, no.
I prov'd back in the day.

00:08:55.534 --> 00:08:57.469
I don't prov anymore.
I don't like watching it.

00:08:57.469 --> 00:08:58.770
I don't like doing it.
-Okay.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:00.205
-But did you ever --
When you were young,

00:09:00.205 --> 00:09:01.874
did you ever get to improvise
with your dad?

00:09:01.874 --> 00:09:04.843
-Yes, the story goes,
I was three years old.

00:09:04.843 --> 00:09:07.646
-Three?
-Yeah, my mom was either

00:09:07.646 --> 00:09:10.182
that or that, I don't remember.

00:09:10.182 --> 00:09:13.018
And I would go to San Francisco
with my dad to improv,

00:09:13.018 --> 00:09:17.123
and I would run on the stage
when the scenes were happening.

00:09:17.123 --> 00:09:19.892
They take it very seriously
in San Francisco.

00:09:19.892 --> 00:09:21.760
-Yeah.
-So he lifted me off.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.129
I was crying, and my dad's like,
"Do you want a cookie?"

00:09:24.129 --> 00:09:27.400
And then I just went, "I just
want to finish my scene."

00:09:27.400 --> 00:09:29.201
[ Laughter ]

00:09:29.201 --> 00:09:30.502
And here we are.

00:09:30.502 --> 00:09:32.204
-You were like,
"The stage is my cookie!"

00:09:32.204 --> 00:09:34.840
-My stage!
-"The stage is my cookie!"

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:37.877
-Yeah.
-Well, your instinct was right.

00:09:37.877 --> 00:09:40.579
And it's very sweet that he gave
that space for you.

00:09:40.579 --> 00:09:41.847
-It's very cool.

00:09:41.847 --> 00:09:43.682
He's in an Audible podcast
I'm doing,

00:09:43.682 --> 00:09:47.186
and he just got his S.A.G. card,
so watch out, world.

00:09:47.186 --> 00:09:48.954
-Watch out, world.

00:09:48.954 --> 00:09:50.256
Hey, thank you so much
for being here.

00:09:50.256 --> 00:09:51.556
-Yeah, thank you.
-We really appreciate it.

00:09:51.556 --> 00:09:52.958
Congrats on the season.
-Thank you for having me.

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:54.326
-Chloe Fineman, everybody.

00:09:54.326 --> 00:09:57.229
"Father of the Bride" premieres
June 16th on HBO Max.

00:09:57.229 --> 00:09:58.230
We'll be right back.

